	(text "Precharge and contactor"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 20 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "28bda69f-69a7-4898-8cf1-113ac0df18cf")
	)
	(text "Precharge relay + resistor, main contactor command, passive bleeder, active discharge. SPEC.md 7 - DECISIONS.md D013/D014/D016."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "33b52022-08fe-45e6-8329-608492dbfbce")
	)
	(text "K401 = Hongfa HFE80V-20C/450-12-HTPAJ (orderable ordering code; the Value field previously held a description).\nCoil is in the LV 12 V domain, contacts switch the HV DC bus - the relay itself is the isolation barrier and must\nbe rated for it: HV DC precharge relay, >= 450 V DC contact rating, 20 A. K401 never breaks load (verified\nreview 2). Coil suppression: D401 + D404, see the coil-suppression note."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 33 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8d3ccc0d-5701-4009-8507-1a2c89c12fce")
	)
	(text "R401 precharge resistor - CORRECTED (D025 / SPEC 7.1). This note previously assumed a 400 uF bank; it is 500 uF.\nE = 0.5 x C x V^2 = 0.5 x 500u x 450^2 = 50.6 J (53.2 J at C +5 %), and 62.5 J when precharging from a 500 V rail\n-> requirement is >= 65 J single-shot, NOT the >= 41 J previously printed here.\nPart: Ohmite/ARCOL HS50 1K2 J - 1.2k +/-5 % wirewound, aluminium housed, chassis mount, 1250 V limiting element\nvoltage (2.8x over 450 V), 3500 Vpk / 2500 Vrms insulation, 200 C max hot spot.\nRATING CAVEAT: 50 W applies ONLY bolted to ~535 cm2 x 3.0 mm Al with thermal compound; in free air it is 14 W.\nSingle-shot: the published overload envelope (5 x P for 5 s = 1250 J, 10 x P for 1 s = 500 J) covers 65 J with\n>= 7.7x margin. Ohmite publishes no explicit joule rating for HS10-HS300 [TBV if >= 65 J becomes a qualification\nrequirement rather than design margin - get it in writing].\n1.25k -> 1.2k (nearest stocked): tau = 1.2k x 500u = 0.60 s, 5 tau = 3.0 s (firmware timeout >= 3.2 s still valid),\npeak inrush 450/1200 = 0.375 A, peak dissipation 169 W = 3.4 x rated - inside the 5x-for-5 s envelope."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 86 172 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "282c51bf-7d07-4c25-acda-a1b20940f2d0")
	)
	(text "Main contactor is external to this board - only the coil command is generated here.\nCONTACTOR_P / CONTACTOR_N feed the external coil from +12 V, flyback-protected (SPEC 13). Closure only per SPEC 7.1 sequencing."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 136.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b8da5d00-642a-42d9-893d-3d4b2efffff6")
	)
	(text "Passive bleeder: series string, >= 4 resistors per SPEC 8.2 - no single part may span 450 V.\nCORRECTED (D025 / review 3 MJ-11): 4 x 18.7k = 74.8k gave tau = 37.4 s and 75.4 s from 450 V to 60 V - it FAILED\nSPEC 7.2's own < 60 s requirement by 26 %. Now 4 x 14k = 56k: tau = 56k x 500 uF = 28.0 s,\nt(450 -> 60 V) = 28.0 x ln(450/60) = 56.4 s. 3.6 W total at 450 V; 0.90 W and 112.5 V per part.\nPart: Stackpole RMCP2512FT14K0 - 2512 thick film, 2 W, 250 V max element voltage / 500 V overload, +/-1 %.\nWorking-voltage check: sqrt(P x R) = sqrt(2 x 14000) = 167 V > 112.5 V, and 112.5 V < the 250 V element limit;\npower loading 0.90 / 2 = 45 %.\nDEVIATION FROM D025, deliberate: D025 wrote '3 W 2512'. No 14k 3 W 2512 is stocked anywhere (Stackpole\nRMCP2512-UP and Bourns CHP2512 are both 22-23 week / MOQ 3000-4000 factory orders, and the -UP 3 W figure is\nonly in DigiKey parametrics, not in the datasheet). 3 W is not needed: the binding constraint is\nsqrt(P x R) >= 112.5 V, which the stocked 2 W part clears by 1.49x."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160 41 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "dccbd164-ac97-4f73-a756-6be3ed6d361e")
	)
	(text "Active discharge (SPEC 7.2): R421-R424, 4 x 220R = 880R, in series with Q403 (C3M0350120J, 1200 V SiC).\n~0.51 A initial at 450 V, ~230 W initial pulse for < 5 s - single-shot thermal rating [TBV], not continuous.\nSeries string per SPEC 8.2 - no single resistor spans 450 V.\nHARDWARE-INHIBITED (SPEC 7.2 / D025 / review 3 MJ-12): see the DISCHARGE_DRV interlock below. Asserting\nDISCHARGE_EN while CONTACTOR_EN is asserted would otherwise put 230 W into a 100 W bank indefinitely across a\nlive 450 V bus, with nothing but firmware between the two GPIOs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 55.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "47145e53-b3ae-4032-ad4e-b9eeef7c8dba")
	)
	(text "Q403 gate drive - VOM1271 photovoltaic driver, no supply needed. Rds elevated at ~8 V VGS (not spec'd below\n11 V) - acceptable for current-limited single-shot duty (D022 research).\nR427 100R -> 220R (review 2 MJ-5 / MN-4): at 100R the LED drew I_F = 17-21 mA from an STM32F405 pin whose\ncharacterisation point is 8 mA and whose absolute maximum is 25 mA, leaving V_OC / I_SC indeterminate. The LED is\nnow driven by U402 (see interlock), V_OH ~ 3.15 V at 8 mA: I_F = (3.15 - 1.25)/220 = 8.6 mA (7.3-9.8 mA over\nV_F 1.1-1.4 V and V_OH 3.0-3.25 V) - on the datasheet's characterised operating point.\nD403 MM3Z18VT1G -> 15 V (review 2 MJ-3): the 18 V part is 17.1-18.9 V at I_ZT, so it clamps ABOVE the FET's\n+19 V transient V_GS maximum and never inside the +15 V operating maximum. A 15 V part (14.3-15.8 V at I_ZT)\nclamps inside the operating maximum and stays above the ~8-11 V normal photovoltaic drive so it steals nothing\nfrom the uA-class source.\nMILLER CLAMP Q404/C421/R428 (review 2 MJ-1): C_rss/C_iss = 3.4/345 pF means a 450 V drain step injects\n450 x C_rss,eff/(C_rss,eff + C_iss) on the gate - 4.4 V at the datasheet 3.4 pF and worse once C_rss rises at low\nV_DS - against V_GS(th) min 1.8 V. The only pull-downs were R426 10M (tau 3.45 ms) and the VOM1271's uA-class\ninternal turn-off (~112 us equivalent): both are 4-5 orders of magnitude too slow.\nC421 1 nF couples the gate step onto Q404's gate (1 nF against Ciss 27 pF -> the clamp gate sees 97 % of it) and\nR428 10k holds Q404 off statically (tau 10 us hold-time after an event; the legitimate VOM1271 turn-on ramp is\nms-class, so it cannot trigger the clamp). Q404 = BSS138, V_GS(th) 0.8/1.3/1.5 V, so the clamp fires while Q403's\ngate is still at ~1.34 V typ / 1.54 V worst case - below V_GS(th) min 1.8 V.\nRESPONSE TIME: BSS138 t_d(on) 2.5 ns + t_r 9 ns = 11.5 ns typ; the gate then discharges through R_DS(on)\n(1.0 R typ / 6.0 R max at 4.5 V) into C_iss 345 pF, tau = 0.35-2.1 ns. Total < 15 ns from threshold crossing,\nagainst a dv/dt event measured in tens of ns. The VOM1271 drive path (R425 47R) is untouched."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 86 250 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a42a2bb9-7d8e-4939-ab6a-0355f5ee8396")
	)
	(text "SPEC 7.1 sequencing rule:\n\"precharge relay closes -> bus monitored -> main contactor closes only when V_bus >= 95% of supply -> precharge relay\nopens. The MCU commands both; neither may close without a valid bus voltage reading.\""
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 106.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
