	(text "DISCHARGE INTERLOCK - SPEC 7.2 / D025 / review 3 MJ-12 (was CRITICAL C2).
DISCHARGE_EN (PE4) and CONTACTOR_EN (PE3) were independent GPIOs with nothing between them.
U402 = TI SN74LVC1G97DBVR configurable gate, SOT-23-6, 1.65-5.5 V, tpd 6.3 ns max at 3.3 V, +/-24 mA,
Schmitt inputs, Ioff. Its function is Y = /IN2 . IN1 + IN2 . IN0 (a 2:1 mux, IN2 = select).
TYING IN0 (pin 3) TO GND gives Y = IN1 . NOT(IN2) - SCES416N Table 2 / Figure 6.
  IN1 = DISCHARGE_EN (pin 1), IN2 = CONTACTOR_EN (pin 6), Y = DISCHARGE_DRV (pin 4) -> R427 -> U401 LED.

  DISCHARGE_EN  CONTACTOR_EN  DISCHARGE_DRV   result
       0             0             0          idle
       0             1             0          contactor closed, discharge not commanded
       1             0             1          DISCHARGE PERMITTED (contactor commanded open)
       1             1             0          INHIBITED IN HARDWARE - the 230 W / 100 W case

R429 10k pull-down on DISCHARGE_EN (was missing): holds the request de-asserted through reset and boot, before
the MCU GPIO is initialised. CONTACTOR_EN already had R405 10k. At power-up +3.3 V rises with both inputs low,
so Y is low and the VOM1271 LED is dark - fail-safe.
SELF-CONTAINED: this does NOT depend on the spare U903 gate on the supervisor sheet.
C420 100 nF local decoupling at U402 pin 5."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196 95 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "cb701cf3-cede-4c69-bdbe-c329dc42e613")
	)
	(text "COIL SUPPRESSION - review 3 C4/MN-5 and D025 (contactor coil is 1.7-2.5 A, SPEC 11.2, a requirement not an
assumption).
D401/D402 were BAS316: 250 mA I_F(AV), 500 mA I_FRM. D402 saw the full 1.7-2.5 A coil current on the first
contactor drop-out - it fails, and takes Q402 with it. D401 sat at exactly its 250 mA rating.
  D401 -> ES1G   (SMA / DO-214AC, 400 V, 1.0 A I_F(AV), 30 A I_FSM 8.3 ms, t_rr 35 ns) - K401 coil
  D402 -> ES2G   (Taiwan Semiconductor, SMB / DO-214AA, 400 V, 2.0 A, 50 A I_FSM, t_rr 35 ns) - external
                 contactor coil. Specify the MANUFACTURER: several vendors ship 'ES2G' in SMA, not SMB.
DIODE + SERIES TVS, not a plain diode (Hongfa application note): a plain freewheel diode clamps the coil at
~0.9 V, which stretches release time and reduces contact life. D404/D405 = SMBJ24A unidirectional TVS in
anti-series with the rectifier - the pair blocks DC (rectifier reverse-biased) and clamps the flyback at
V_BR + V_F. SMBJ24A: V_RWM 24 V (clear of a +10 % 12 V rail), V_BR 26.7-29.5 V at 1 mA, V_C 38.9 V at 15.5 A;
interpolating R_d = 0.607 R gives ~29-31 V at the 2.5 A coil current, so the switch node reaches
12 + 31 + 1.3 = ~44 V. Release time improves ~30x (t ~ L.I/V: 125 ms at 1 V -> 4.2 ms at 30 V).
Energy at L = 50 mH, 2.5 A: E = 0.156 J, t = 2.9 ms, peak 109 W = 18 % of the SMBJ 600 W rating; SMB single-pulse
capability ~0.60 J -> 26 % utilisation. ACTION: measure the real coil inductance at bring-up - at L = 200 mH,
E = 0.625 J would exceed SMB and force an SMC part.
CONSEQUENCE, deliberate: the ~44 V clamp is above AO3400A's 30 V V_DS, so Q401/Q402 are re-rated (see values).
A zener cannot be used in place of the TVS: 1SMA5936B / 1SMB5931B publish no I_ZSM and no peak-power-vs-pulse
curve, and 2.5 A is 50x their DC I_ZM - their clamp voltage at coil current is unbounded by the datasheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196 220 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "56d3718b-0c97-468f-9a07-3a9ef996ec53")
	)

	(text "COIL DRIVER RE-RATING - consequence of the diode+TVS clamp above, NOT an independent change.
Q401/Q402 were AO3400A, V_DS 30 V. With a SMBJ24A clamping at V_BR 26.7-29.5 V (and up to ~32 V at 2.5 A)
plus the series rectifier V_F, the drain of each low-side switch now rests at rail + ~30-32 V during coil
release: ~44 V at a nominal 12 V rail, ~48-50 V worst case on a 16 V rail. The 30 V parts would avalanche
on every drop-out.
  Q401 -> onsemi NVR5198NLT1G, SOT-23, 60 V, V_GS(th) 1.5-2.5 V, R_DS(on) 205 mR max at V_GS 4.5 V,
       I_D 1.7 A cont. K401 coil is 3 W / 250 mA at 12 V (48 R, no economiser; ~440 mA worst case at a
       16 V rail and -40 C coil): P = 0.0128 W nominal / ~0.05 W worst case, dT_j = +1.8 / +7 C on
       R_thJA 139 C/W. ~4x current and ~70x power margin.
  Q402 -> Diodes DMN6068LK3-13, TO-252 (DPAK), 60 V, R_DS(on) 100 mR max at V_GS 4.5 V / 6 A,
       I_D 6.0 A steady state, E_AS 37.5 mJ. At the 2.5 A contactor coil P = 0.70 W and dT_j = +21 C on a
       50x50 mm 2 oz drain pour (R_thJA 30.3 C/W). LAYOUT REQUIREMENT: on a 25x25 mm 1 oz pour R_thJA is
       59 C/W -> +49 C, and at 85 C ambient T_j ~ 145 C. Give the tab a >= 50x50 mm-equivalent 2 oz pour or
       stitched inner-layer copper. SOT-23 is not an option here: the best 60 V SOT-23 (NVR5198NL, 205 mR)
       would dissipate ~1.3 W against a 0.9 W package.
RESIDUAL RISK, recorded: worst case ~48-50 V on a 60 V part is only ~17 % margin. Measure the actual clamp
voltage at 0.25 A and 2.5 A at bring-up; if the rail can excurse above 16 V, move to 100 V parts."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196 258 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "caae593e-88ec-471c-8c28-7e0ca728bc8c")
	)

	(embedded_fonts no)
)
